{"thought": "TEE must NOT be dead when today<=40 but must be dead when today=60. So a no-shipment SKU becomes dead only once enough time has passed since it was stocked: idle measured from its last restock (max RCV/RTN day on/before today). MUG's SHP@50>today40 means it recently moved out → not dead. Let me implement: no SHP on/before today → dead iff today - last_restock >= idle; else use last SHP.", "action": {"tool": "edit_file", "args": {"path": "src/stockflow/dead_stock.py", "old": "    # Most recent shipment day per SKU (all SHP records, regardless of date).
    last_ship: Dict[str, int] = {}
    for line in kept_lines:
        rec = parse_movement_line(line, case_sizes)
        if rec["type"] != "SHP":
            continue
        day = rec["day"]
        sku = rec["sku"]
        if sku not in last_ship or day > last_ship[sku]:
            last_ship[sku] = day

    result: List[str] = []
    for sku, qty in total_on_hand.items():
        if qty <= 0:
            continue
        last = last_ship.get(sku)
        # Dead stock: no shipment at all, or the most recent shipment is
        # at least idle_days days old (a shipment dated after `today` is not
        # yet idle).
        if last is None or today - last >= idle_days:
            result.append(sku)

    return sorted(result)", "new": "    # Most recent shipment day per SKU, counting only movements up to and
    # including `today`.
    last_ship: Dict[str, int] = {}
    # Most recent restock (RCV/RTN) day per SKU, also up to and including today.
    last_restock: Dict[str, int] = {}
    for line in kept_lines:
        rec = parse_movement_line(line, case_sizes)
        day = rec["day"]
        if day > today:
            continue
        sku = rec["sku"]
        mtype = rec["type"]
        if mtype == "SHP":
            if sku not in last_ship or day > last_ship[sku]:
                last_ship[sku] = day
        elif mtype in ("RCV", "RTN"):
            if sku not in last_restock or day > last_restock[sku]:
                last_restock[sku] = day

    result: List[str] = []
    for sku, qty in total_on_hand.items():
        if qty <= 0:
            continue
        if sku in last_ship:
            # Recently moved out: idle since the most recent shipment.
            if today - last_ship[sku] >= idle_days:
                result.append(sku)
        else:
            # No shipment on/before today: stock has sat since it was last
            # restocked; idle once that restock is at least idle_days old.
            restock = last_restock.get(sku)
            if restock is not None and today - restock >= idle_days:
                result.append(sku)

    return sorted(result)"}}, "messages": []}

